---
source: crates/mori-checker/src/tests.rs
description: "Code:\n\nprofile \"moriarty-beta/1\";\nagreement Ids {\n  domain Preview = { id: \"preview\", chain: \"midnight\", network: \"preview\" };\n  domain Mainnet = { id: \"main\", chain: \"midnight\", network: \"main\" };\n  account alice = { domain: Preview, id: \"alice\" };\n  account alice2 = { domain: Preview, id: \"alice\" };\n  account alice_main = { domain: Mainnet, id: \"alice\" };\n  account bad = { domain: Preview, id: \"not-valid\" };\n  account reserved = { domain: Preview, id: \"transfer\" };\n}\n"
---
mori::check::duplicate_id

  × Another account on `Preview` already has the id `alice`.
   ╭─[test.mori:6:43]
 4 │   domain Mainnet = { id: "main", chain: "midnight", network: "main" };
 5 │   account alice = { domain: Preview, id: "alice" };
   ·                                          ───┬───
   ·                                             ╰── first used here
 6 │   account alice2 = { domain: Preview, id: "alice" };
   ·                                           ───┬───
   ·                                              ╰── used again here
 7 │   account alice_main = { domain: Mainnet, id: "alice" };
   ╰────
  help: Each economic identity is declared once. Refer to the existing
        declaration instead of declaring an alias.

mori::check::invalid_id

  × The id `not-valid` cannot be used in Source/6.
   ╭─[test.mori:8:40]
 7 │   account alice_main = { domain: Mainnet, id: "alice" };
 8 │   account bad = { domain: Preview, id: "not-valid" };
   ·                                        ─────┬─────
   ·                                             ╰── not a valid Source/6 id
 9 │   account reserved = { domain: Preview, id: "transfer" };
   ╰────
  help: Ids start with an ASCII letter, continue with letters, digits or `_`,
        are at most 64 characters, and avoid Source/6's reserved words.

mori::check::invalid_id

  × The id `transfer` cannot be used in Source/6.
    ╭─[test.mori:9:45]
  8 │   account bad = { domain: Preview, id: "not-valid" };
  9 │   account reserved = { domain: Preview, id: "transfer" };
    ·                                             ─────┬────
    ·                                                  ╰── not a valid Source/6 id
 10 │ }
    ╰────
  help: Ids start with an ASCII letter, continue with letters, digits or `_`,
        are at most 64 characters, and avoid Source/6's reserved words.
